    <summaries>
      <summary>
        <versionCode>00</versionCode>
        <actionDate>2025-05-05</actionDate>
        <actionDesc>Introduced in Senate</actionDesc>
        <updateDate>2026-11-17T14:21:09Z</updateDate>
        <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Aviation Workforce Development Act </strong></p><p>This bill expands the&nbsp;qualified higher education expenses that may be paid for with tax-free distributions from a qualified tuition program (also known as a 529 plan) to include expenses (e.g., tuition, fees, books, supplies, and equipment) for&nbsp;aviation maintenance or commercial pilot courses taught at schools&nbsp;certified by the Federal Aviation Administration.</p><p>Under current law, 529 plan distributions are excluded from gross income, for federal tax purposes, if they are used to pay for qualified higher education expenses.</p>]]></text>
      </summary>
    </summaries>
